> API and interpretation

The original ten-key sample uses insertion sort entirely at the default cutoff;
the report does not label a separately reconstructed histogram as its radix
history. The8000-word figure reads the actual root histogram. Counters exclude
allocation, bound checks and internal timing. Fixed32-bit keys allow at most
four byte levels, while fallback comparisons and per-pass256-entry prefix work
are counted separately.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

